    "blurb": "Father and son live above this modest second-hand bookshop on Santa Anna Street, between the Rambla and Portal de l’Àngel.",
    "notesByBeat": [
      {
        "beatId": "empty-catalogues",
        "text": "Daniel searches his father’s catalogues for Julián Carax and finds nothing — not even a rumour."
      },
      {
        "beatId": "watching-street",
        "text": "Back in their rooms, Daniel tells his father he has promised to read to Clara, then asks about the war, and is told it is better left alone."
      },
      {
        "beatId": "empty-birthday",
        "text": "Daniel is sixteen. The dinner is laid for Clara and Barceló. Only Bernarda sits down."
      },
      {
        "beatId": "birthday-pen",
        "text": "After midnight his father is still awake. The fountain pen from the old shop window is the birthday gift."
      },
      {
        "beatId": "fermin-hired",
        "text": "Fermín is brought in from the street. There are scars. Mr. Sempere offers him a job."
      },
      {
        "beatId": "burned-photo",
        "text": "Someone leaves a half-burned photograph: a young couple, and a window that says Sons of Antonio Fortuny."
      },
      {
        "beatId": "fumero-counter",
        "text": "Inspector Fumero stands at the counter and asks after Fermín. Daniel says he does not know him."
      },
      {
        "beatId": "bea-card",
        "text": "Bea leaves a card and is gone before he opens it. The address is already known to him."
      },
      {
        "beatId": "shop-smashed",
        "text": "Fumero turns the shelves. Tomorrow’s paper will do worse."
      },
      {
        "beatId": "nuria-paris",
        "text": "Daniel reads the first pages here, behind a shut door."
      },
      {
        "beatId": "a-wedding-anyway",
        "text": "The shop becomes a house again. There will be a child with a borrowed name."
      }
    ],
